{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1197209-boon-evaluation","id":1197209,"title":"Boon Evaluation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-19T08:33:33-07:00","id":1197209,"title":"Boon Evaluation","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> Let me start off by saying that I loved the leaked information regarding Aedes and Boons! However, I wanted to evaluate these boons and maybe the community can help me understand some of these boons and their benefits. Below are my evaluations thus far of the boons provided:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Death of Magic (Death): The Angel may completely dispel any magic with a dot rating (i.e. Merit rating, Arcanum level of a spell, etc.) equal to or lower than its Rank. Its touch can also remove a dot of Gnosis from a mage if it succeeds in a contested action. If the mage is reduced to 0 Gnosis, she becomes a Sleepwalker. </div> </div> </div>Great Boon! Everything about it is fantastic!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Grace of the Sword (Fate): The Angel may raise (or lower) the dot rating of an Artifact by a value equal to its Rank. A given Artifact may only benefit from this Boon once, though a second application can be used to restore its original rating. </div> </div> </div>Another great boon, definitely something that cannot be achieved by a mere mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Scouring (Forces): One of the most terrifying Boons, this power allows an Angel to unleash a divine storm of such magnitude and ferocity that it effectively destroys an area with a diameter equal to the being's Rank in miles. The destruction takes at least a day (forty days and nights is more traditional), during which time the area is lashed with whatever Environmental Tilts the Storyteller deems appropriate. Those within the area have a chance to escape, but even with a large-scale, concerted evacuation effort, many people will die. Angels reserve their most arduous Trials for those mages who would ask them to invoke this power, and never do so for any reason they deem unvirtuous. </div> </div> </div>Alright, this is my first questionable boon that could be replicated by real magic. My best guess as to why you would want this boon is my assumption it can't be unraveled by sleepers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Living Mana (Life): The Angel may grant dots in any Physical Merit, or create or cure a number of Conditions or Tilts relating to physical health (including Blinded, Deafened, Poisoned, or Sick), equal to its Rank. It may mix and match these effects; a Rank 3 Angel might cure Blinded, inflict Arm Wrack, and grant a dot in a Physical Merit, for example. </div> </div> </div>Hm... this one is fairly weak, can't a mage already do this? I assume this is the &quot;Regrow your limb&quot; boon that used to be in Summoners, which is kind of neat I suppose assuming the effects cannot be unraveled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sword of Righteousness (Matter): The Angel may craft an Artifact that falls under its primary Arcanum's purview. The Artifact has a Merit rating of 3 + the Angel's Rank. A mage can only receive one such Boon from the Angels, and if she uses it in any way that contradicts her Virtue or the tenets of Wisdom as she understands them, she earns the wrath of the Aether. Any angel can perceive her and affect her as though she were using Focused Mage Sight. Only by undertaking a significant ritual of purification can she return to Heaven's graces. </div> </div> </div>Another great boon!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tutelary Wisdom (Mind): The Angel may grant a number of Mental Skill dots equal to its Rank to a mage with a single touch. These Skill dots last until the end of the story. </div> </div> </div>Hm... a 3-dot spell. Not a great boon here that I can reason in any form or fashion. I mean the lengthy duration is nice, but can easily be done by a Mage, not worth spending the mana to summon a supernal entity. If you have insight on this, please let me know in the comments below as to why this boon is good. I suppose if it can't be dispelled by another mage it is nice, but is such a situational thing and doesn't seem to be something you would want to spend a lot of time trying to get an entity to give you this boon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Revelation (Prime): The Angel may make visible to any mage with Active Mage Sight all ley lines, nodes, and Hallows within a number of miles equal to the entity's Rank. Any Mystery related to the flows of magical energy has its Opacity reduced by the Angel's Rank; if this reduces a Mystery's Opacity to 0, the Mystery is obvious to any mage who cares to Reveal it. </div> </div> </div>A good boon, maybe not as beneficial as some others but a solid one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Scepter of Heaven (Space): The angel may grant a mage a scepter of authority which may be used as a representational sympathy Yantra for any Space spell. The mage must still<br /> have a sympathetic connection to cast a spell at sympathetic range. The scepter may be used as a Yantra a number of times equal to the Angel's Rank before it returns to the Supernal World. </div> </div> </div>A fantastic boon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Word of Binding (Spirit): The Angel may levy a new ban on any spirit present, or on any spirit whose name it knows. For purposes of this Boon, a spirit's name is the appellation it's known by in the language of spirits. The new ban's severity is based off of the Angel's Rank, not the spirit's (a Rank 4 Angel levies a severe Ban, even on a Rank 2 spirit). If the spirit is higher Rank than the Angel, this provokes a Clash of Wills. </div> </div> </div>A great boon and definitely helpful for Shamans that are spirit weak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Angel of the Hours (Time): The Angel may send a number of individuals equal to its Rank through time to a specific hour (e.g. 6 in the morning on October 23, 1874). Each Angel has dominion over a single, specific hour; when that hour is up, the subjects return to the present. Any changes made in the past are permanent. </div> </div> </div>This is a cool boon.<br /> <br /> For the most part you can tell that I find most of them pretty good, but there are a few that really escape me as to why they are so great, seems mages can already do some of these things on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T08:44:30-07:00","id":1197213,"title":"","content":"Well, obviously these are just examples, not every Angel of Prime and Life is going to have a Boon that removes permanent physical Conditions. Though, that one is pretty good considering it\u2019s the equivalent of a Lasting Regeneration.<br /> <br /> Scouring by the way, what you have to consider there is the Scale. It exceeds the upper limits that Mages can achieve on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T08:55:02-07:00","id":1197220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, obviously these are just examples, not every Angel of Prime and Life is going to have a Boon that removes permanent physical Conditions. Though, that one is pretty good considering it\u2019s the equivalent of a Lasting Regeneration.<br /> <br /> Scouring by the way, what you have to consider there is the Scale. It exceeds the upper limits that Mages can achieve on their own. </div> </div> </div>Well, Scouring can't be done by a single mage but a group could accomplish this from my understanding, which is usually how supernal entities are summoned. However, for the lone mage this is powerful again assuming it can't be unraveled by Sleepers. That is the key point, I have to assume all of these things are immune to being unraveled despite Supernal Beings suffering paradoxes with Sleeper witnesses. Kind of an odd thing we have going on here with them as in their magic can suffer paradox but their boons (maybe?) do not.<br /> <br /> Yes, that was my take on the Life Boon assuming it can't be unraveled or dispelled.<br /> <br /> I noticed you didn't touch the mind one, and I realize these are examples, but that one seems pretty weak. I think a better example for Mind would have been the following:<br /> <br /> Mind Reader (Mind): All spells that involve perceiving knowledge from Sleepers are able to bypass any withstand, but those protected by Mind spells suffer a clash of wills with the mage attacker receiving the die pool of Gnosis + Supernal Entity's Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T11:14:40-07:00","id":1197270,"title":"","content":"The mind one isn't bad at all. It's a free boost in skill dots that doesn't cost you anything, no upkeep, no dispellation, etc. You seem to assume that every Supernal Entity and their boons have to be of worldshaking power, but they really don't have to be. And as Mrmdubois said those are only examples anyway. The important detail when homebrewing up additional ones is I think staying in theme with the realm. You Mind Reader for example sounds more like something a Demon would give out to me. For Angels I could rather see something that reveals the aspiration of every person the Mage sees for a few days or until the end of the story, showing you their inspiration (rather than their hidden flaws and secret thoughts as a Demon would.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T12:09:13-07:00","id":1197286,"title":"","content":"Hey Flinty,<br /> <br /> I agree it is not a terrible deal, but this was also something we had in Summoners already. I was looking for different effects than those rehashed from 1E. Maybe the book will provide more I just expected something \u201cunique\u201d.<br /> <br /> Granted there are no Rank assignments/system mentioned other than the trial so maybe getting a boost to a Mental Skill is not a big deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Autocorrect from phone can sometimes be annoying. 03-19-2018, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T13:21:12-07:00","id":1197304,"title":"","content":"It will provide more, Dave specifically said these were the ones they came up with for the Obrimos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T13:21:45-07:00","id":1197305,"title":"","content":"One thing to also remember is that the Life boon can grant Physical Merits and that it's not apparently time-limited, so you might consider it a Lasting effect and not even have to pay the experience cost for the merit. And if Life Angels can do that, there is nothing thematically wrong with Mind Angels granting Lasting Mental/Social Merits. I'm less sure if Life Angels can grant Physical Skills, Mind Angels grant Social Skills etc.; and if they could do it as a Lasting effect (the same with an alternate boon granting Lasting Mental skills). For the Lasting effect, the Mind boon points at &quot;no&quot;, but there may be differences between summoned Angels or their strength in Rank that could allow for that option.<br /> <br /> We would probably need Dave's comment to clarify how much leeway do we have in modifying the examples, while creating our own boons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T05:19:56-07:00","id":1197565,"title":"","content":"I agree, I look forward to this book with each passing day. I will totally pay a king's ransom once it is released. Thanks for your input everyone, I suppose I was leery of the boons until every reaffirmed my understanding that these Boons would work very similar to 1E in that they would not be subject to any Dissonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}